hit disk need to be encrypted, and it has to work with no network dependency.\\n\\n**[2026-08-03 11:30] Charlie**: Any library lean yet?\\n\\n**[2026-08-03 11:48] Bob**: Evaluating options for AES-256 that fit the offline runtime. Want something we can ship without cloud KMS.\\n\\n**[2026-08-03 13:45] Diana**: Application-level on the outputs, or wrapping the whole volume?\\n\\n**[2026-08-03 13:54] Bob**: Application-level on the redacted outputs. More portable across the workstations we're targeting.\\n\\n**[2026-08-03 14:03] Alice**: Keep the eval focused on AES-256 at rest for local outputs. Implementation can follow once you've picked a library path.\\n\\n**[2026-08-03 14:40] Bob**: Will do. Next step after this is wiring the pipeline once the library choice is settled.\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"sourc id src slack 20 slack thread local encrypt at rest crypto evalu channel cipherdoc date 2026 08 03 2026 08 03 11 02 bob start on local encrypt at rest redact output that hit disk need to be encrypt and it ha to work with no network depend 2026 08 03 11 30 charli ani librari lean yet 2026 08 03 11 48 bob evalu option for ae 256 that fit the offlin runtim want someth we can ship without cloud km 2026 08 03 13 45 diana applic level on the output or wrap the whole volum 2026 08 03 13 54 bob applic level on the redact output more portabl across the workstat we re target 2026 08 03 14 03 alic keep the eval focus on ae 256 at rest for local output implement can follow onc you ve pick a librari path 2026 08 03 14 40 bob will do next step after this is wire the pipelin onc the librari choic is settl\", \"dataset_id\": \"918880948a9911f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"edc587768a9911f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-08-03-aes256-crypto-eval.md\", \"id\": \"0d8a3376fd7823f3\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.2728248089978772, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.08817491999696743, \"vector_similarity\": 0.70367455, \"dataset_name\": \"C1WR-2\", \"document_name\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-08-03-aes256-crypto-eval.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"edc587768a9911f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-08-03-aes256-crypto-eval.md\", \"location\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-08-03-aes256-crypto-eval.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 992, \"chunk_count\": 1, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:35:14\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:09:11\", \"token_count\": 299, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"918880948a9911f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"**Source ID**: SRC-SLACK-26\\n\\n# Slack Thread: Node Sync Handshake Prototype\\n\\n**Channel**: #cipherdoc\\n\\n**Date**: 2026-08-06\\n\\n---\\n\\n**[2026-08-06 09:30] Bob**: Starting on the replication handshake for the zero-trust node sync. First requirement is that two nodes have to authenticate each other before either one accepts replicated entries.\\n\\n**[2026-08-06 09:37] Evan**: How's a node proving who it is right now?\\n\\n**[2026-08-06 09:38] Bob**: Each node has a registered identity it presents at connect time. If the peer doesn't recognize it, the connection gets dropped before any data moves.\\n\\n**[2026-08-06 09:49] Charlie**: Does the handshake add noticeable overhead to the redaction jobs running on the same box?\\n\\n**[2026-08-06 10:40] Bob**: Negligible so far — it's a short exchange before the sync session opens, nothing that touches the active redaction path.\\n\\n**[2026-08-06 10:41] Diana**: What's next after the prototype?\\n\\n**[2026-08-06 11:47] Bob**: Need to check it holds up under real network delay, not just on my two test nodes on the same switch. That's the next pass.\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"sourc id src slack 26 slack thread node sync handshak prototyp channel cipherdoc date 2026 08 06 2026 08 06 09 30 bob start on the replic handshak for the zero trust node sync first requir is that two node have to authent each other befor either one accept replic entri 2026 08 06 09 37 evan how s a node prove who it is right now 2026 08 06 09 38 bob each node ha a regist ident it present at connect time if the peer doesn t recogn it the connect get drop befor ani data move 2026 08 06 09 49 charli doe the handshak add notic overhead to the redact job run on the same box 2026 08 06 10 40 bob neglig so far it s a short exchang befor the sync session open noth that touch the activ redact path 2026 08 06 10 41 diana what s next after the prototyp 2026 08 06 11 47 bob need to check it hold up under real network delay not just on my two test node on the same switch that s the next pas\", \"dataset_id\": \"918880948a9911f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"ede2c2fa8a9911f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-08-06-node-sync-handshake-prototype.md\", \"id\": \"4bd5b5740e6d4a32\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.2638655351095682, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.0748285215850974, \"vector_similarity\": 0.7049519, \"dataset_name\": \"C1WR-2\", \"document_name\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-08-06-node-sync-handshake-prototype.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"ede2c2fa8a9911f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-08-06-node-sync-handshake-prototype.md\", \"location\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-08-06-node-sync-handshake-prototype.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 1079, \"chunk_count\": 1, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:35:15\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:08:46\", \"token_count\": 317, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"918880948a9911f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"**Source ID**: SRC-SLACK-58\\n\\n# Slack Thread: High-DPI Upstream Block\\n\\n**Channel**: #cipherdoc\\n\\n**Date**: 2026-09-10\\n\\n---\\n\\n**[2026-09-10 10:41] Diana**: Bad news on the high-DPI rendering fix. The rotation fix Charlie pushed works for simple cases, but it's completely breaking on documents with nested Form XObjects.\\n\\n**[2026-09-10 10:43] Charlie**: Yeah, I looked into it. The underlying rendering library we're using (`pdf-lib-core`) has a known bug in how it handles coordinates for XObjects when a parent transform is applied.\\n\\n**[2026-09-10 10:55] Alice**: Can we patch it?\\n\\n**[2026-09-10 10:56] Charlie**: No.\\n\\n**[2026-09-10 11:35] Charlie**: It's deep in their C++ core. I've opened an issue with the upstream maintainers, but they haven't responded.\\n\\n**[2026-09-10 11:37] Evan**: We can't wait for an upstream fix if we're hitting the release gate. Can we work around it by flattening the PDFs first?\\n\\n**[2026-09-10 11:51] Charlie**: Flattening might work but it'll blow up the file size and we might lose some text layers.\\n\\n**[2026-09-10 12:29] Alice**: @Diana, @Charlie, let's leave high-DPI rendering blocked for now. We need to decide if we can ship with this limitation or if we need a different rendering library entirely.\\n\\n**[2026-09-10 12:32] Diana**: Agreed. It only affects a small subset of complex documents, but we should document it as a known issue.\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"sourc id src slack 58 slack thread high dpi upstream block channel cipherdoc date 2026 09 10 2026 09 1010 41 diana bad news on the high dpi render fix the rotat fix charli push work for simpl case but it s complet break on document with nest form xobject 2026 09 1010 43 charli yeah i look into it the under render librari we re use pdf lib core ha a known bug in how it handl coordin for xobject when a parent transform is appli 2026 09 1010 55 alic can we patch it 2026 09 1010 56 charli no 2026 09 10 11 35 charli it s deep in their c core i ve open an issu with the upstream maintain but they haven t respond 2026 09 10 11 37 evan we can t wait for an upstream fix if we re hit the releas gate can we work around it by flatten the pdfs first 2026 09 10 11 51 charli flatten might work but it ll blow up the file size and we might lose some text layer 2026 09 10 12 29 alic diana charli let s leav high dpi render block for now we need to decid if we can ship with this limit or if we need a differ render librari entir 2026 09 10 12 32 diana agre it onli affect a small subset of complex document but we should document it a a known issu\", \"dataset_id\": \"918880948a9911f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"ee20a43a8a9911f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-09-10-high-dpi-upstream-block.md\", \"id\": \"66a2899f0f7ec51f\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.2545943351095682, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.0748285215850974, \"vector_similarity\": 0.6740479, \"dataset_name\": \"C1WR-2\", \"document_name\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-09-10-high-dpi-upstream-block.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"ee20a43a8a9911f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-09-10-high-dpi-upstream-block.md\", \"location\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-09-10-high-dpi-upstream-block.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 1371, \"chunk_count\": 1, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:35:15\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:07:47\", \"token_count\": 414, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"918880948a9911f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"**Source ID**: SRC-SLACK-49\\n\\n# Slack Thread: Memory Leak Tracemalloc Patch\\n\\n**Channel**: #cipherdoc\\n\\n**Thread opened**: 2026-08-21\\n\\n**Last activity**: 2026-08-23\\n\\n---\\n\\n**[2026-08-21 09:00] Charlie**: Switching to `tracemalloc` for the leak hunt since the usual profiler is a no-go on the offline lab box. Kicking off a fresh capture now.\\n\\n**[2026-08-21 11:05] Charlie**: Already got something. The `tracemalloc` output shows we're holding onto the full page-tree in `RedactionEngine` even after the document object is closed.\\n\\n**[2026-08-21 11:50] Bob**: That lines up with the hotspot list from earlier this week. I'll start on a patch tonight.\\n\\n**[2026-08-23 09:45] Bob**: Patch is in. Added explicit cleanup so the context manager actually releases the page-tree reference instead of just closing the file handle.\\n\\n**[2026-08-23 09:47] Diana**: Just finished a 6-hour soak test with the new build. Memory usage is flat as a pancake after the initial load. :pancake:\\n\\n**[2026-08-23 10:41] Alice**: Huge relief. Is this on top of the buffer-release fix from the large-file chunking rework, or a separate code path?\\n\\n**[2026-08-23 10:43] Bob**: Same family of fix — builds on the chunking buffer-release work. PR #84 is merged.\\n\\n**[2026-08-23 10:44] Evan**: On it.\\n\\n**[2026-08-23 10:46] Evan**: Rolling this out to the dev clusters. @Charlie thanks for the tracemalloc deep dive.\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"sourc id src slack 49 slack thread memori leak tracemalloc patch channel cipherdoc thread open 2026 08 21 last activ 2026 08 23 2026 08 21 09 00 charli switch to tracemalloc for the leak hunt sinc the usual profil is a no go on the offlin lab box kick off a fresh captur now 2026 08 21 11 05 charli alreadi got someth the tracemalloc output show we re hold onto the full page tree in redactionengin even after the document object is close 2026 08 21 11 50 bob that line up with the hotspot list from earlier this week i ll start on a patch tonight 2026 08 23 09 45 bob patch is in ad explicit cleanup so the context manag actual releas the page tree refer instead of just close the file handl 2026 08 23 09 47 diana just finish a 6 hour soak test with the new build memori usag is flat a a pancak after the initi load pancak 2026 08 23 10 41 alic huge relief is this on top of the buffer releas fix from the larg file chunk rework or a separ code path 2026 08 23 10 43 bob same famili of fix build on the chunk buffer releas work pr 84 is merg 2026 08 23 10 44 evan on it 2026 08 23 10 46 evan roll this out to the dev cluster charli thank for the tracemalloc deep dive\", \"dataset_id\": \"918880948a9911f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"edd405b28a9911f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-08-21-memory-leak-tracemalloc.md\", \"id\": \"a0cc2b5fe938c85d\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.25456990610956814, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.0748285215850974, \"vector_similarity\": 0.67396647, \"dataset_name\": \"C1WR-2\", \"document_name\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-08-21-memory-leak-tracemalloc.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"edd405b28a9911f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-08-21-memory-leak-tracemalloc.md\", \"location\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-08-21-memory-leak-tracemalloc.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 1379, \"chunk_count\": 1, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:35:14\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:08:55\", \"token_count\": 428, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"918880948a9911f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"**Source ID**: SRC-SLACK-43\\n\\n# Slack Thread: Large File Chunking Reopen\\n\\n**Channel**: #cipherdoc\\n\\n**Date**: 2026-08-18\\n\\n---\\n\\n**[2026-08-18 10:30] Bob**: Reopening large-file chunking. On long-running batches with files over 2GB, memory is still leaking even though the chunked-read path is supposedly done.\\n\\n**[2026-08-18 10:31] Charlie**: That's odd, chunking should mean each buffer gets dropped once we move past it.\\n\\n**[2026-08-18 10:41] Bob**: It's not the page buffers themselves — something else is holding a reference and keeping them from being freed.\\n\\n**[2026-08-18 11:08] Diana**: I can reproduce it in QA too. Memory climbs steadily and the process eventually gets killed on the larger inputs.\\n\\n**[2026-08-18 11:20] Charlie**: I'll dig into what's still holding those references. Reopening this until we find it.\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"sourc id src slack 43 slack thread larg file chunk reopen channel cipherdoc date 2026 08 18 2026 08 18 10 30 bob reopen larg file chunk on long run batch with file over 2gb memori is still leak even though the chunk read path is suppos done 2026 08 18 10 31 charli that s odd chunk should mean each buffer get drop onc we move past it 2026 08 18 10 41 bob it s not the page buffer themselv someth els is hold a refer and keep them from be freed 2026 08 18 11 08 diana i can reproduc it in qa too memori climb steadili and the process eventu get kill on the larger input 2026 08 18 11 20 charli i ll dig into what s still hold those refer reopen this until we find it\", \"dataset_id\": \"918880948a9911f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"ee0cc0a08a9911f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-08-18-large-file-chunking-reopen.md\", \"id\": \"fc180423f1c2406b\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.2535415151095682, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.0748285215850974, \"vector_similarity\": 0.6705385, \"dataset_name\": \"C1WR-2\", \"document_name\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-08-18-large-file-chunking-reopen.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"ee0cc0a08a9911f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-08-18-large-file-chunking-reopen.md\", \"location\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-08-18-large-file-chunking-reopen.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 825, \"chunk_count\": 1, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:35:15\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:08:06\", \"token_count\": 252, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"918880948a9911f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"**Source ID**: SRC-SLACK-61\\n\\n# Slack Thread: Async Batch I/O Race\\n\\n**Channel**: #cipherdoc\\n\\n**Date**: 2026-08-25\\n\\n---\\n\\n**[2026-08-25 10:20] Diana**: Blocker on the async batch path. Under concurrent load the workers hit an I/O race and throughput drops — roughly 10% versus the sync baseline.\\n\\n**[2026-08-25 10:21] Bob**: Is that the scheduler shell or the workers we just added?\\n\\n**[2026-08-25 10:23] Diana**: The workers. Scheduler alone was fine; once concurrent workers share I/O with the existing multi-thread batch pool, the race shows up.\\n\\n**[2026-08-25 11:48] Charlie**: That pool is the multi-thread path. Mixing it with async workers without coordinating I/O was going to bite us.\\n\\n**[2026-08-25 12:50] Alice**: Then we stop here. I have to leave the async batch work blocked until the race with the multi-thread pool is sorted. A 10% hit is not shippable.\\n\\n**[2026-08-25 12:51] Bob**: Ok.\\n\\n**[2026-08-25 12:52] Bob**: Fair. I'll hold further async work until we understand the interaction with that pool.\\n\\n**[2026-08-25 12:54] Diana**: I'll capture the repro steps so we can re-run once there's a candidate fix.\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"sourc id src slack 61 slack thread async batch i o race channel cipherdoc date 2026 08 25 2026 08 25 10 20 diana blocker on the async batch path under concurr load the worker hit an i o race and throughput drop rough 10 versus the sync baselin 2026 08 25 10 21 bob is that the schedul shell or the worker we just ad 2026 08 25 10 23 diana the worker schedul alon wa fine onc concurr worker share i o with the exist multi thread batch pool the race show up 2026 08 25 11 48 charli that pool is the multi thread path mix it with async worker without coordin i o wa go to bite u 2026 08 25 12 50 alic then we stop here i have to leav the async batch work block until the race with the multi thread pool is sort a 10 hit is not shippabl 2026 08 25 12 51 bob ok 2026 08 25 12 52 bob fair i ll hold further async work until we understand the interact with that pool 2026 08 25 12 54 diana i ll captur the repro step so we can re run onc there s a candid fix\", \"dataset_id\": \"918880948a9911f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"ee1d78008a9911f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-08-25-async-batch-io-race.md\", \"id\": \"d35a1fb74d2e1aff\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.25279656522125915, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.061482123173227356, \"vector_similarity\": 0.69919693, \"dataset_name\": \"C1WR-2\", \"document_name\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-08-25-async-batch-io-race.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"ee1d78008a9911f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-08-25-async-batch-io-race.md\", \"location\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-08-25-async-batch-io-race.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 1123, \"chunk_count\": 1, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:35:15\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:07:49\", \"token_count\": 349, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"918880948a9911f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}], \"pagination\": {\"page\": 1, \"page_size\": 10, \"total_chunks\": 70, \"total_pages\": 7}, \"query_info\": {\"question\": \"SRC-MEET-11 high latency simulation timeout encryption path stabilization timeout bump workaround\", \"similarity_threshold\": 0.2, \"vector_weight\": 0.3, \"keyword_search\": false, \"dataset_count\": 1}}"}],"structured_content":null},"error":null,"status":"completed"}}
