{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_5","type":"mcp_tool_call","server":"tl-v1","tool":"ragflow_retrieval","arguments":{"dataset_ids":["918880948a9911f197db2303d7337e37"],"question":"Node Sync Handshake Validation 2026-08-08 nominal-latency handshake validation passed high-latency simulation September 22","page_size":10,"vector_similarity_weight":0.3,"similarity_threshold":0.2,"top_k":1024,"keyword":false,"metadata_condition":{"logic":"and","conditions":[{"name":"path","comparison_operator":"is","value":"sources"}]}},"result":{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"{\"chunks\": [{\"content\": \"**Source ID**: SRC-SLACK-27\\n\\n# Slack Thread: Node Sync Handshake Validation\\n\\n**Channel**: #cipherdoc\\n\\n**Thread opened**: 2026-08-08\\n\\n**Last activity**: 2026-09-22\\n\\n---\\n\\n**[2026-08-08 09:04] Bob**: Ran the handshake validation under nominal latency — two nodes on the local network, dozens of connect attempts back to back. No failures.\\n\\n**[2026-08-08 09:05] Evan**: Any dropped or retried handshakes at all?\\n\\n**[2026-08-08 09:30] Bob**: None. Every attempt authenticated cleanly on the first try at this latency.\\n\\n**[2026-08-08 09:32] Diana**: We still need the high-latency case covered before this goes anywhere near the field.\\n\\n**[2026-08-08 09:38] Bob**: Agreed, it's next on the list. First cut of the nominal-latency pass looks solid — leaving it in progress until we cover high latency.\\n\\n**[2026-08-08 09:41] Diana**: Good.\\n\\n**[2026-09-22 09:50] Diana**: Reopening this. Ran the handshake over a simulated high-latency link and it's timing out — never completes the exchange.\\n\\n**[2026-09-22 10:08] Bob**: Timing out, or actively failing? Could just be the round trip budget being too tight.\\n\\n**[2026-09-22 10:09] Diana**: Times out. And it gets worse the slower the link — feels like the handshake is doing more work per round trip than it should.\\n\\n**[2026-09-22 10:18] Bob**: That tracks. The AES-256 pipeline we added on the output path adds per-packet overhead, and on a slow link that pushes the exchange past the timeout window. This depends on the encryption work settling down before we can retest — handshake work stays blocked for now.\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"sourc id src slack 27 slack thread node sync handshak valid channel cipherdoc thread open 2026 08 08 last activ 2026 09 22 2026 08 08 09 04 bob ran the handshak valid under nomin latenc two node on the local network dozen of connect attempt back to back no failur 2026 08 08 09 05 evan ani drop or retri handshak at all 2026 08 08 09 30 bob none everi attempt authent clean on the first tri at this latenc 2026 08 08 09 32 diana we still need the high latenc case cover befor this go anywher near the field 2026 08 08 09 38 bob agre it s next on the list first cut of the nomin latenc pas look solid leav it in progress until we cover high latenc 2026 08 08 09 41 diana good 2026 09 22 09 50 diana reopen this ran the handshak over a simul high latenc link and it s time out never complet the exchang 2026 09 22 10 08 bob time out or activ fail could just be the round trip budget be too tight 2026 09 22 10 09 diana time out and it get wors the slower the link feel like the handshak is do more work per round trip than it should 2026 09 22 1018 bob that track the ae 256 pipelin we ad on the output path add per packet overhead and on a slow link that push the exchang past the timeout window this depend on the encrypt work settl down befor we can retest handshak work stay block for now\", \"dataset_id\": \"918880948a9911f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"ee16ca328a9911f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-08-08-node-sync-handshake-validation.md\", \"id\": \"4951fb04269a3c9b\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.5295715944251425, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.3895956634644894, \"vector_similarity\": 0.8561821, \"dataset_name\": \"C1WR-2\", \"document_name\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-08-08-node-sync-handshake-validation.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"ee16ca328a9911f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-08-08-node-sync-handshake-validation.md\", \"location\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-08-08-node-sync-handshake-validation.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 1559, \"chunk_count\": 1, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:35:15\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:07:57\", \"token_count\": 450, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"918880948a9911f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"**Source ID**: SRC-GDOC-38\\n\\n# Node Sync Handshake Prototype — Architecture Note\\n\\n**Owner**: Bob\\n\\n**Document Key**: DOC-2038\\n\\n**Last Updated**: 2026-08-15 (retrospective, covers 2026-08-06)\\n\\nMulti-site local deployments need authenticated node sync without assuming a shared network password. T024 opened for a distributed zero-trust sync path; the first concrete deliverable was a replication handshake between peers.\\n\\n## Prototype (2026-08-06)\\n\\nBob implemented a node-replication handshake so each side must authenticate before accepting sync traffic from the other. That put an Active prototype on the board for T024.\\n\\n**Source ID**: SRC-GDOC-38\\n\\n# Node Sync Handshake Prototype — Architecture Note\\n\\n**Owner**: Bob\\n\\n**Document Key**: DOC-2038\\n\\n**Last Updated**: 2026-08-15 (retrospective, covers 2026-08-06)\\n\\nMulti-site local deployments need authenticated node sync without assuming a shared network password. T024 opened for a distributed zero-trust sync path; the first concrete deliverable was a replication handshake between peers.\\n\\n## What this note does not claim\\n\\nNominal-latency validation and any later high-latency failure modes are outside this write-up. As of 2026-08-06 the task was Active on the strength of the prototype alone.\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"sourc id src gdoc 38 node sync handshak prototyp architectur note owner bob document key doc 2038 last updat 2026 08 15 retrospect cover 2026 08 06 multi site local deploy need authent node sync without assum a share network password t024 open for a distribut zero trust sync path the first concret deliver wa a replic handshak between peer prototyp 2026 08 06 bob implement a node replic handshak so each side must authent befor accept sync traffic from the other that put an activ prototyp on the board for t024 sourc id src gdoc 38 node sync handshak prototyp architectur note owner bob document key doc 2038 last updat 2026 08 15 retrospect cover 2026 08 06 multi site local deploy need authent node sync without assum a share network password t024 open for a distribut zero trust sync path the first concret deliver wa a replic handshak between peer what this note doe not claim nomin latenc valid and ani later high latenc failur mode are outsid this write up a of 2026 08 06 the task wa activ on the strength of the prototyp alon\", \"dataset_id\": \"918880948a9911f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"eeb58bfe8a9911f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"med-synth/documentation/sources/2026-08-15-Zero-Trust-Node-Sync-Architecture-Review.md\", \"id\": \"7e1255c3936201b2\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.4328082789259979, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.27072846989428273, \"vector_similarity\": 0.8109945, \"dataset_name\": \"C1WR-2\", \"document_name\": \"med-synth/documentation/sources/2026-08-15-Zero-Trust-Node-Sync-Architecture-Review.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"eeb58bfe8a9911f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"med-synth/documentation/sources/2026-08-15-Zero-Trust-Node-Sync-Architecture-Review.md\", \"location\": \"med-synth/documentation/sources/2026-08-15-Zero-Trust-Node-Sync-Architecture-Review.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 825, \"chunk_count\": 1, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:35:16\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:05:35\", \"token_count\": 313, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"918880948a9911f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"# ClickUp Task: CIPH-34\\n\\n**Source ID**: SRC-CU-CIPH-34\\n\\n**Task ID**: CIPH-34\\n\\n**Title**: Authenticated handshake for multi-site node sync\\n\\n**Status**: Blocked\\n\\n**Assignee**: Bob\\n\\n**Priority**: High\\n\\n**Date Created**: 2026-08-04\\n\\n## Description\\n\\nEnable distributed zero-trust node synchronization for multi-site local deployments, requiring an authenticated handshake between nodes. Validation of the handshake under high-latency networks failed with timeouts; the fix depends on the completed encryption work, but the task remains blocked pending resolution.\\n\\n# ClickUp Task: CIPH-34\\n\\n**Source ID**: SRC-CU-CIPH-34\\n\\n**Task ID**: CIPH-34\\n\\n**Title**: Authenticated handshake for multi-site node sync\\n\\n**Status**: Blocked\\n\\n**Assignee**: Bob\\n\\n**Priority**: High\\n\\n**Date Created**: 2026-08-04\\n\\n## Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n- Authenticated node-replication handshake completes reliably between nodes.\\n\\n- Handshake succeeds under high-latency network conditions, not only nominal latency.\\n\\n- Blocking timeout issue is resolved before multi-site rollout can proceed.\\n\\n# ClickUp Task: CIPH-34\\n\\n**Source ID**: SRC-CU-CIPH-34\\n\\n**Task ID**: CIPH-34\\n\\n**Title**: Authenticated handshake for multi-site node sync\\n\\n**Status**: Blocked\\n\\n**Assignee**: Bob\\n\\n**Priority**: High\\n\\n**Date Created**: 2026-08-04\\n\\n## Description\\n\\nEnable distributed zero-trust node synchronization for multi-site local deployments, requiring an authenticated handshake between nodes. Validation of the handshake under high-latency networks failed with timeouts; the fix depends on the completed encryption work, but the task remains blocked pending resolution.\\n\\n# ClickUp Task: CIPH-34\\n\\n**Source ID**: SRC-CU-CIPH-34\\n\\n**Task ID**: CIPH-34\\n\\n**Title**: Authenticated handshake for multi-site node sync\\n\\n**Status**: Blocked\\n\\n**Assignee**: Bob\\n\\n**Priority**: High\\n\\n**Date Created**: 2026-08-04\\n\\n## Activity History\\n\\n- **2026-08-04**: Alice - Task Create (Open)\\n\\n - *Opened the task because multi-site local deployments need distributed zero-trust node synchronization.*\\n\\n- **2026-09-22**: Diana - Handshake Timeout Block (Blocked)\\n\\n - *Blocked after validation showed handshake timeouts on high-latency networks; resolution depends on the encryption work but remains unresolved.*\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"clickup task ciph 34 sourc id src cu ciph 34 task id ciph 34 titl authent handshak for multi site node sync status block assigne bob prioriti high date creat 2026 08 04 descript enabl distribut zero trust node synchron for multi site local deploy requir an authent handshak between node valid of the handshak under high latenc network fail with timeout the fix depend on the complet encrypt work but the task remain block pend resolut clickup task ciph 34 sourc id src cu ciph 34 task id ciph 34 titl authent handshak for multi site node sync status block assigne bob prioriti high date creat 2026 08 04 accept criterion authent node replic handshak complet reliabl between node handshak succeed under high latenc network condit not onli nomin latenc block timeout issu is resolv befor multi site rollout can proceed clickup task ciph 34 sourc id src cu ciph 34 task id ciph 34 titl authent handshak for multi site node sync status block assigne bob prioriti high date creat 2026 08 04 descript enabl distribut zero trust node synchron for multi site local deploy requir an authent handshak between node valid of the handshak under high latenc network fail with timeout the fix depend on the complet encrypt work but the task remain block pend resolut clickup task ciph 34 sourc id src cu ciph 34 task id ciph 34 titl authent handshak for multi site node sync status block assigne bob prioriti high date creat 2026 08 04 activ histori 2026 08 04 alic task creat open open the task becaus multi site local deploy need distribut zero trust node synchron 2026 09 22 diana handshak timeout block block block after valid show handshak timeout on high latenc network resolut depend on the encrypt work but remain unresolv\", \"dataset_id\": \"918880948a9911f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"ee7fcda28a9911f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"med-synth/tasks/CIPH-34-Zero-Trust-Node-Sync.md\", \"id\": \"75c816de63af91e2\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.42211038450636557, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.2769898778662365, \"vector_similarity\": 0.7607249, \"dataset_name\": \"C1WR-2\", \"document_name\": \"med-synth/tasks/CIPH-34-Zero-Trust-Node-Sync.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"ee7fcda28a9911f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"med-synth/tasks/CIPH-34-Zero-Trust-Node-Sync.md\", \"location\": \"med-synth/tasks/CIPH-34-Zero-Trust-Node-Sync.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 1197, \"chunk_count\": 1, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:35:16\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:06:21\", \"token_count\": 534, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"918880948a9911f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"**Source ID**: SRC-GDOC-18\\n\\n# Zero-Trust Node Sync: Handshake Prototype Notes\\n\\n**Owner**: Bob\\n\\n**Document Key**: DOC-2018\\n\\n**Last Updated**: 2026-08-15 (retrospective, covers 2026-08-06)\\n\\nThis note looks back at the first authenticated handshake prototype built 2026-08-06 for CIPH-34 (Zero-Trust Node Sync), ahead of multi-site local deployments.\\n\\n## What was prototyped\\n\\nA handshake in which each node presents a signed challenge/response before either side accepts replication traffic from the other. No central node is required to bootstrap trust between two peers.\\n\\n**Source ID**: SRC-GDOC-18\\n\\n# Zero-Trust Node Sync: Handshake Prototype Notes\\n\\n**Owner**: Bob\\n\\n**Document Key**: DOC-2018\\n\\n**Last Updated**: 2026-08-15 (retrospective, covers 2026-08-06)\\n\\nThis note looks back at the first authenticated handshake prototype built 2026-08-06 for CIPH-34 (Zero-Trust Node Sync), ahead of multi-site local deployments.\\n\\n## Result as of 2026-08-06\\n\\nThe handshake completed reliably across every run on a single LAN segment with nominal round-trip latency. No cross-node encryption mismatches or handshake rejections were seen at that stage.\\n\\n**Source ID**: SRC-GDOC-18\\n\\n# Zero-Trust Node Sync: Handshake Prototype Notes\\n\\n**Owner**: Bob\\n\\n**Document Key**: DOC-2018\\n\\n**Last Updated**: 2026-08-15 (retrospective, covers 2026-08-06)\\n\\nThis note looks back at the first authenticated handshake prototype built 2026-08-06 for CIPH-34 (Zero-Trust Node Sync), ahead of multi-site local deployments.\\n\\n## Open question\\n\\nThe prototype has only been exercised on one LAN segment. Whether the handshake holds up across a simulated multi-site link with realistic latency and jitter has not been tested and is the planned next step before this can support multi-site rollout.\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"sourc id src gdoc 18 zero trust node sync handshak prototyp note owner bob document key doc 2018 last updat 2026 08 15 retrospect cover 2026 08 06 this note look back at the first authent handshak prototyp built 2026 08 06 for ciph 34 zero trust node sync ahead of multi site local deploy what wa prototyp a handshak in which each node present a sign challeng respons befor either side accept replic traffic from the other no central node is requir to bootstrap trust between two peer sourc id src gdoc 18 zero trust node sync handshak prototyp note owner bob document key doc 2018 last updat 2026 08 15 retrospect cover 2026 08 06 this note look back at the first authent handshak prototyp built 2026 08 06 for ciph 34 zero trust node sync ahead of multi site local deploy result a of 2026 08 06 the handshak complet reliabl across everi run on a singl lan segment with nomin round trip latenc no cross node encrypt mismatch or handshak reject were seen at that stage sourc id src gdoc 18 zero trust node sync handshak prototyp note owner bob document key doc 2018 last updat 2026 08 15 retrospect cover 2026 08 06 this note look back at the first authent handshak prototyp built 2026 08 06 for ciph 34 zero trust node sync ahead of multi site local deploy open question the prototyp ha onli been exercis on one lan segment whether the handshak hold up across a simul multi site link with realist latenc and jitter ha not been test and is the plan next step befor this can support multi site rollout\", \"dataset_id\": \"918880948a9911f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"eec9d0788a9911f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"med-synth/documentation/sources/2026-08-15-Zero-Trust-Node-Sync-Review.md\", \"id\": \"93691740b3cc2cb4\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.410744518884119, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.23460368412017, \"vector_similarity\": 0.8217398, \"dataset_name\": \"C1WR-2\", \"document_name\": \"med-synth/documentation/sources/2026-08-15-Zero-Trust-Node-Sync-Review.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"eec9d0788a9911f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"med-synth/documentation/sources/2026-08-15-Zero-Trust-Node-Sync-Review.md\", \"location\": \"med-synth/documentation/sources/2026-08-15-Zero-Trust-Node-Sync-Review.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 1055, \"chunk_count\": 1, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:35:16\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:05:18\", \"token_count\": 453, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"918880948a9911f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"**Source ID**: SRC-SLACK-26\\n\\n# Slack Thread: Node Sync Handshake Prototype\\n\\n**Channel**: #cipherdoc\\n\\n**Date**: 2026-08-06\\n\\n---\\n\\n**[2026-08-06 09:30] Bob**: Starting on the replication handshake for the zero-trust node sync. First requirement is that two nodes have to authenticate each other before either one accepts replicated entries.\\n\\n**[2026-08-06 09:37] Evan**: How's a node proving who it is right now?\\n\\n**[2026-08-06 09:38] Bob**: Each node has a registered identity it presents at connect time. If the peer doesn't recognize it, the connection gets dropped before any data moves.\\n\\n**[2026-08-06 09:49] Charlie**: Does the handshake add noticeable overhead to the redaction jobs running on the same box?\\n\\n**[2026-08-06 10:40] Bob**: Negligible so far — it's a short exchange before the sync session opens, nothing that touches the active redaction path.\\n\\n**[2026-08-06 10:41] Diana**: What's next after the prototype?\\n\\n**[2026-08-06 11:47] Bob**: Need to check it holds up under real network delay, not just on my two test nodes on the same switch. That's the next pass.\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"sourc id src slack 26 slack thread node sync handshak prototyp channel cipherdoc date 2026 08 06 2026 08 06 09 30 bob start on the replic handshak for the zero trust node sync first requir is that two node have to authent each other befor either one accept replic entri 2026 08 06 09 37 evan how s a node prove who it is right now 2026 08 06 09 38 bob each node ha a regist ident it present at connect time if the peer doesn t recogn it the connect get drop befor ani data move 2026 08 06 09 49 charli doe the handshak add notic overhead to the redact job run on the same box 2026 08 06 10 40 bob neglig so far it s a short exchang befor the sync session open noth that touch the activ redact path 2026 08 06 10 41 diana what s next after the prototyp 2026 08 06 11 47 bob need to check it hold up under real network delay not just on my two test node on the same switch that s the next pas\", \"dataset_id\": \"918880948a9911f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"ede2c2fa8a9911f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-08-06-node-sync-handshake-prototype.md\", \"id\": \"4bd5b5740e6d4a32\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.3916041974196513, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.2036395820280733, \"vector_similarity\": 0.8301883, \"dataset_name\": \"C1WR-2\", \"document_name\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-08-06-node-sync-handshake-prototype.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"ede2c2fa8a9911f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-08-06-node-sync-handshake-prototype.md\", \"location\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-08-06-node-sync-handshake-prototype.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 1079, \"chunk_count\": 1, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:35:15\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:08:46\", \"token_count\": 317, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"918880948a9911f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"**Source ID**: SRC-MEET-11\\n\\n# Fireflies Transcript: Handshake Protocol Deep Dive\\n\\n**Date**: 2026-09-22\\n\\n**Participants**: Alice (PM), Bob (Backend), Charlie (Engine), Diana (QA), Evan (DevOps)\\n\\n## Summary\\n\\nDiana walked the high-latency handshake timeout. The team left handshake work blocked; no timeout-bump workaround. Path still depends on the encryption workstream.\\n\\n**Source ID**: SRC-MEET-11\\n\\n# Fireflies Transcript: Handshake Protocol Deep Dive\\n\\n**Date**: 2026-09-22\\n\\n**Participants**: Alice (PM), Bob (Backend), Charlie (Engine), Diana (QA), Evan (DevOps)\\n\\n## Transcript\\n\\n**Diana**: Handshake triage — nominal latency was fine; Bob's earlier validation held up on the local network. On a simulated high-latency link the handshake never finishes. It times out.\\n\\n**Bob**: That matches what I expected once we left the happy path. The prototype assumed round trips stay quick. High latency breaks the exchange.\\n\\n**Charlie**: Is this an encryption cost problem? AES-256 on the wire path is in the dependency chain here.\\n\\n**Bob**: It's related. The handshake still has to complete under that load, and on a slow link it doesn't. I don't have a fix that keeps the current exchange as-is.\\n\\n**Evan**: Bumping timeouts just hides it. If the link is slow enough, we still fail.\\n\\n**Diana**: I'll leave the high-latency repro in place so we can re-check when encryption or the handshake design changes.\\n\\n**Alice**: Then we leave it. Handshake work stays blocked on timeouts under high latency. It depends on the encryption path, and we're not inventing a workaround in this meeting.\\n\\n**Bob**: Agreed — no timeout bump. We'll revisit when the crypto path moves.\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"sourc id src meet 11 firefli transcript handshak protocol deep dive date 2026 09 22 particip alic pm bob backend charli engin diana qa evan devop summari diana walk the high latenc handshak timeout the team left handshak work block no timeout bump workaround path still depend on the encrypt workstream sourc id src meet 11 firefli transcript handshak protocol deep dive date 2026 09 22 particip alic pm bob backend charli engin diana qa evan devop transcript diana handshak triag nomin latenc wa fine bob s earlier valid held up on the local network on a simul high latenc link the handshak never finish it time out bob that match what i expect onc we left the happi path the prototyp assum round trip stay quick high latenc break the exchang charli is this an encrypt cost problem ae 256 on the wire path is in the depend chain here bob it s relat the handshak still ha to complet under that load and on a slow link it doesn t i don t have a fix that keep the current exchang ais evan bump timeout just hide it if the link is slow enough we still fail diana i ll leav the high latenc repro in place so we can re check when encrypt or the handshak design chang alic then we leav it handshak work stay block on timeout under high latenc it depend on the encrypt path and we re not invent a workaround in this meet bob agre no timeout bump we ll revisit when the crypto path move\", \"dataset_id\": \"918880948a9911f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"ee2d56f88a9911f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/fireflies/2026-09-22-Handshake-Protocol-Deep-Dive.md\", \"id\": \"756514b50ae50d73\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.35689913973649845, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.17250401105214064, \"vector_similarity\": 0.78715444, \"dataset_name\": \"C1WR-2\", \"document_name\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/fireflies/2026-09-22-Handshake-Protocol-Deep-Dive.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"ee2d56f88a9911f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/fireflies/2026-09-22-Handshake-Protocol-Deep-Dive.md\", \"location\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/fireflies/2026-09-22-Handshake-Protocol-Deep-Dive.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 1463, \"chunk_count\": 1, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:35:15\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:07:33\", \"token_count\": 417, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"918880948a9911f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"**Source ID**: SRC-GDOC-22\\n\\n# Benchmark Script Authoring Notes\\n\\n**Owner**: Evan\\n\\n**Document Key**: DOC-2022\\n\\n**Last Updated**: 2026-08-17 (retrospective, covers 2026-08-07)\\n\\nLooking back at the bare-metal benchmark work under CIPH-38, from where the scripting started.\\n\\n## What was authored on 2026-08-07\\n\\nA set of repeatable benchmark scripts intended to produce bare-metal performance numbers for release performance claims. The scripts run a fixed batch of documents through the CLI and record throughput and latency percentiles.\\n\\n**Source ID**: SRC-GDOC-22\\n\\n# Benchmark Script Authoring Notes\\n\\n**Owner**: Evan\\n\\n**Document Key**: DOC-2022\\n\\n**Last Updated**: 2026-08-17 (retrospective, covers 2026-08-07)\\n\\nLooking back at the bare-metal benchmark work under CIPH-38, from where the scripting started.\\n\\n## What happened after authoring\\n\\nOnce written, the scripts sat blocked for a stretch while a dedicated bare-metal node was provisioned — they weren't written to target shared or virtualized hardware, since noisy neighbors would make the numbers unusable for a release claim. They were rerun once that node became available, and results were published depending on the completed multi-threading baseline.\\n\\n**Source ID**: SRC-GDOC-22\\n\\n# Benchmark Script Authoring Notes\\n\\n**Owner**: Evan\\n\\n**Document Key**: DOC-2022\\n\\n**Last Updated**: 2026-08-17 (retrospective, covers 2026-08-07)\\n\\nLooking back at the bare-metal benchmark work under CIPH-38, from where the scripting started.\\n\\n## Scope of this note\\n\\nThis note is about the scripts themselves and why they were written the way they were; it is not a report on the published benchmark numbers.\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"sourc id src gdoc 22 benchmark script author note owner evan document key doc 2022 last updat 2026 08 17 retrospect cover 2026 08 07 look back at the bare metal benchmark work under ciph 38 from where the script start what wa author on 2026 08 07 a set of repeat benchmark script intend to produc bare metal perform number for releas perform claim the script run a fix batch of document through the cli and record throughput and latenc percentil sourc id src gdoc 22 benchmark script author note owner evan document key doc 2022 last updat 2026 08 17 retrospect cover 2026 08 07 look back at the bare metal benchmark work under ciph 38 from where the script start what happen after author onc written the script sat block for a stretch while a dedic bare metal node wa provis they weren t written to target share or virtual hardwar sinc noisi neighbor would make the number unus for a releas claim they were rerun onc that node becam avail and result were publish depend on the complet multi thread baselin sourc id src gdoc 22 benchmark script author note owner evan document key doc 2022 last updat 2026 08 17 retrospect cover 2026 08 07 look back at the bare metal benchmark work under ciph 38 from where the script start scope of this note this note is about the script themselv and whi they were written the way they were it is not a report on the publish benchmark number\", \"dataset_id\": \"918880948a9911f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"eebf09c28a9911f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"med-synth/documentation/sources/2026-08-17-Performance-Benchmarks-Review.md\", \"id\": \"cae008cfb9af56e9\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.34625381584519643, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.19957962263599488, \"vector_similarity\": 0.6884936, \"dataset_name\": \"C1WR-2\", \"document_name\": \"med-synth/documentation/sources/2026-08-17-Performance-Benchmarks-Review.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"eebf09c28a9911f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"med-synth/documentation/sources/2026-08-17-Performance-Benchmarks-Review.md\", \"location\": \"med-synth/documentation/sources/2026-08-17-Performance-Benchmarks-Review.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 1101, \"chunk_count\": 1, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:35:16\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:05:28\", \"token_count\": 409, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"918880948a9911f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"**Source ID**: SRC-SLACK-17\\n\\n# Slack Thread: Offline Auth Mock and Rotation Block\\n\\n**Channel**: #cipherdoc\\n\\n**Thread opened**: 2026-08-04\\n\\n**Last activity**: 2026-08-05\\n\\n---\\n\\n**[2026-08-04 09:14] Bob**: Building the local auth mock for air-gap testing so we can exercise Diana's key-rotation design without a real deployment.\\n\\n**[2026-08-04 09:16] Bob**: Mock is up. It runs the rotation flow with the network disabled, same as a real air-gapped site would see.\\n\\n**[2026-08-04 10:27] Diana**: Good, that's exactly what I need to validate the design against.\\n\\n**[2026-08-05 08:36] Alice**: How'd it go?\\n\\n**[2026-08-05 08:45] Bob**: Not great. Key rotation just can't complete with the network down — the flow we designed assumes at least a brief connection to finish the handshake.\\n\\n**[2026-08-05 08:48] Alice**: Ugh.\\n\\n**[2026-08-05 09:13] Diana**: So we're blocked. There's no resolution yet on how to rotate without any network at all.\\n\\n**[2026-08-05 09:33] Alice**: Offline auth stays blocked. Let's regroup on whether the design needs to change or whether we relax the offline requirement.\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"sourc id src slack 17 slack thread offlin auth mock and rotat block channel cipherdoc thread open 2026 08 04 last activ 2026 08 05 2026 08 04 09 14 bob build the local auth mock for air gap test so we can exercis diana s key rotat design without a real deploy 2026 08 04 09 16 bob mock is up it run the rotat flow with the network disabl same a a real air gap site would see 2026 08 04 10 27 diana good that s exact what i need to valid the design against 2026 08 05 08 36 alic how d it go 2026 08 05 08 45 bob not great key rotat just can t complet with the network down the flow we design assum at least a brief connect to finish the handshak 2026 08 05 08 48 alic ugh 2026 08 05 09 13 diana so we re block there s no resolut yet on how to rotat without ani network at all 2026 08 05 09 33 alic offlin auth stay block let s regroup on whether the design need to chang or whether we relax the offlin requir\", \"dataset_id\": \"918880948a9911f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"edbb698a8a9911f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-08-04-offline-auth-mock-block.md\", \"id\": \"28867d857abb09be\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.3356549859551836, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.17267547993597668, \"vector_similarity\": 0.7159405, \"dataset_name\": \"C1WR-2\", \"document_name\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-08-04-offline-auth-mock-block.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"edbb698a8a9911f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-08-04-offline-auth-mock-block.md\", \"location\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-08-04-offline-auth-mock-block.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 1092, \"chunk_count\": 1, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:35:14\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:09:18\", \"token_count\": 340, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"918880948a9911f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"**Source ID**: SRC-SLACK-16\\n\\n# Slack Thread: Offline Mode Authentication Design\\n\\n**Channel**: #cipherdoc\\n\\n**Date**: 2026-08-02\\n\\n---\\n\\n**[2026-08-02 11:14] Diana**: Starting on offline-mode auth design. If we're running air-gapped, we can't call home for license validation or user auth, so key rotation can't assume an always-on network either.\\n\\n**[2026-08-02 11:16] Alice**: Right — whatever we design has to keep working with no connection for extended stretches.\\n\\n**[2026-08-02 11:22] Diana**: I'm sketching a rotation flow built around a locally held key rather than one that needs a live call to rotate.\\n\\n**[2026-08-02 13:00] Alice**: How do we actually rotate it if the site is air-gapped?\\n\\n**[2026-08-02 14:24] Diana**: Still working that part out — that's the piece I'm least confident about. I'll have a first draft of the design by Wednesday.\\n\\n**[2026-08-02 14:27] Diana**: I'll loop in Bob once the draft's ready so he can start mocking it for testing.\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"sourc id src slack 16 slack thread offlin mode authent design channel cipherdoc date 2026 08 02 2026 08 02 11 14 diana start on offlin mode auth design if we re run air gap we can t call home for licens valid or user auth so key rotat can t assum an alway on network either 2026 08 02 11 16 alic right whatev we design ha to keep work with no connect for extend stretch 2026 08 02 11 22 diana i m sketch a rotat flow built around a local held key rather than one that need a live call to rotat 2026 08 02 13 00 alic how do we actual rotat it if the site is air gap 2026 08 02 14 24 diana still work that part out that s the piec i m least confid about i ll have a first draft of the design by wednesday 2026 08 02 14 27 diana i ll loop in bob onc the draft s readi so he can start mock it for test\", \"dataset_id\": \"918880948a9911f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"ee02ac008a9911f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-08-02-offline-auth-key-rotation.md\", \"id\": \"585e209a330d2aa1\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.33470835153555134, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.17893688790793044, \"vector_similarity\": 0.6981751, \"dataset_name\": \"C1WR-2\", \"document_name\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-08-02-offline-auth-key-rotation.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"ee02ac008a9911f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-08-02-offline-auth-key-rotation.md\", \"location\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-08-02-offline-auth-key-rotation.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 965, \"chunk_count\": 1, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:35:15\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:08:15\", \"token_count\": 291, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"918880948a9911f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"**Source ID**: SRC-SLACK-33\\n\\n# Slack Thread: Offline Batch Run\\n\\n**Channel**: #cipherdoc\\n\\n**Thread opened**: 2026-08-08\\n\\n**Last activity**: 2026-08-10\\n\\n---\\n\\n**[2026-08-08 08:58] Diana**: Harness is ready, so I'm running a full batch through it with the network blocked at the OS level. Kicking off now.\\n\\n**[2026-08-08 11:28] Diana**: Batch is still running clean — no unexpected outbound connection attempts logged so far.\\n\\n**[2026-08-10 09:30] Diana**: Batch finished offline. Signing off, but flagging one thing: there's a roughly 45-second hang at startup where something in the licence check reaches for a remote endpoint before it gives up and falls back to the local path.\\n\\n**[2026-08-10 09:42] Bob**: 45 seconds is a long time to sit there. Is that the encryption-pipeline license check?\\n\\n**[2026-08-10 10:54] Diana**: Looks that way — depends on the encryption work, so I'm not touching that path here. Recording it and moving on.\\n\\n**[2026-08-10 10:56] Alice**: So we're calling this signed off?\\n\\n**[2026-08-10 11:08] Diana**: I'll close this out, but I want to be clear this is a preliminary offline pass — not a compliance certification. The 45-second hang is noted, not resolved.\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"sourc id src slack 33 slack thread offlin batch run channel cipherdoc thread open 2026 08 08 last activ 2026 08 10 2026 08 08 08 58 diana har is readi so i m run a full batch through it with the network block at the o level kick off now 2026 08 08 11 28 diana batch is still run clean no unexpect outbound connect attempt log so far 2026 08 10 09 30 diana batch finish offlin sign off but flag one thing there s a rough 45 second hang at startup where someth in the licenc check reach for a remot endpoint befor it give up and fall back to the local path 2026 08 10 09 42 bob 45 second is a long time to sit there is that the encrypt pipelin licens check 2026 08 1010 54 diana look that way depend on the encrypt work so i m not touch that path here record it and move on 2026 08 1010 56 alic so we re call this sign off 2026 08 10 11 08 diana i ll close this out but i want to be clear this is a preliminari offlin pas not a complianc certif the 45 second hang is note not resolv\", \"dataset_id\": \"918880948a9911f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"ee1382d28a9911f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-08-08-offline-batch-run.md\", \"id\": \"194adb690b85ac78\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.33191612717091257, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.17174622452987512, \"vector_similarity\": 0.7056459, \"dataset_name\": \"C1WR-2\", \"document_name\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-08-08-offline-batch-run.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"ee1382d28a9911f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-08-08-offline-batch-run.md\", \"location\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-08-08-offline-batch-run.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 1193, \"chunk_count\": 1, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:35:15\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:08:01\", \"token_count\": 353, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"918880948a9911f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}], \"pagination\": {\"page\": 1, \"page_size\": 10, \"total_chunks\": 70, \"total_pages\": 7}, \"query_info\": {\"question\": \"Node Sync Handshake Validation 2026-08-08 nominal-latency handshake validation passed high-latency simulation September 22\", \"similarity_threshold\": 0.2, \"vector_weight\": 0.3, \"keyword_search\": false, \"dataset_count\": 1}}"}],"structured_content":null},"error":null,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_6","type":"agent_message","text":"No. The nominal-latency pass is explicitly insufficient for field sign-off.\n\nThe current constraint is that the authenticated handshake must complete reliably on high-latency links—not merely on a LAN/nominal RTT. It currently fails at the Singapore field condition of **180 ms RTT**, so T024/CIPH-34 remains blocked pending encryption-path stabilization and a high-latency retest.\n\nPlanning must assume a **30-second timeout budget** on high-latency links (replacing the failing 5-second prototype budget). [WS-07/T024; CMT-2026-09-004; SRC-SLACK-27]"}}
